Subject: Keep lookupid()'s bsearch() result const

C23 makes bsearch() a generic function that returns a pointer to const
when its base argument points to const. lookupid() searches a const
name_entry_t table and assigns the result to a non-const pointer, which
clang in C23 mode reports as discarding qualifiers; R CMD check counts that
as a significant warning (R-devel compiles C as C23). The entry is only
read, so declare it const, as plutovg-paint.c already does for its
colormap.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §14. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutosvg/source/plutosvg.c
+++ b/plutosvg/source/plutosvg.c
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
         name[i] = data[i];
     name[length] = '\0';
 
-    name_entry_t* entry = bsearch(name, table, count / sizeof(name_entry_t), sizeof(name_entry_t), name_entry_compare);
+    const name_entry_t* entry = bsearch(name, table, count / sizeof(name_entry_t), sizeof(name_entry_t), name_entry_compare);
     if(entry == NULL)
         return 0;
     return entry->id;
